WEBVTT

00:02:44.610 --> 00:02:46.010
Maki...

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:49.470
What have I been doing all this time?

00:02:55.820 --> 00:02:57.510
How weak.

00:02:57.510 --> 00:02:59.150
You’re just a weakling...

00:03:00.420 --> 00:03:02.030
...Takuto Kaneshiro.

00:03:26.420 --> 00:03:29.540
We've increased
the maximum output by 30%.

00:03:29.540 --> 00:03:31.920
It's an actual spec up.

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:36.080
If we cut the limiter,
we can probably get that to 50%.

00:03:37.600 --> 00:03:39.020
Very nice.

00:03:42.500 --> 00:03:45.570
Is that test for your lieutenant's
badge all you care about?

00:03:45.570 --> 00:03:46.580
Huh?

00:03:46.600 --> 00:03:49.040
I'm talking about advancing it a whole class.

00:03:49.370 --> 00:03:53.140
If you break the limit of the inertial eliminator...

00:03:55.050 --> 00:03:56.770
I hear what you're saying.

00:03:56.850 --> 00:04:00.750
The captain and I just don't want
to lose anymore.

00:04:27.210 --> 00:04:31.840
With all these cameras,
we could start our own TV show.

00:04:32.020 --> 00:04:35.350
Of course, this set would
look strange as a TV show.

00:04:35.350 --> 00:04:36.890
You can't help it.

00:04:36.950 --> 00:04:40.390
It’s just that Mr. Fairy and I
have nowhere else to go.

00:04:43.990 --> 00:04:45.330
Hattie.

00:04:45.400 --> 00:04:50.920
Someday, you and Mr. Fairy
can find your own home.

00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:21.530
Dispatch from Moon Base.

00:05:21.600 --> 00:05:23.730
Target passing lunar orbit.

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:26.940
They found that one fast.

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:28.630
Well...

00:05:28.710 --> 00:05:30.760
We have rough stats on the target.

00:05:31.810 --> 00:05:33.690
There's no mistake?

00:05:33.880 --> 00:05:36.310
220 meters high?

00:05:36.380 --> 00:05:40.900
Its mass appears to be about
1000 times that of normal aliens'.

00:05:40.900 --> 00:05:42.860
This is a new one.

00:05:42.860 --> 00:05:45.310
A giant of giants.

00:05:45.390 --> 00:05:48.850
I never imagined there could be one so big.

00:05:48.850 --> 00:05:53.490
Satellite system interception
to commence in 11 minutes.

00:05:53.490 --> 00:05:55.050
This should be an easy one.

00:05:55.050 --> 00:05:56.160
Yes.

00:05:56.230 --> 00:05:58.290
Like throwing darts at a wall.

00:05:58.290 --> 00:06:01.170
Even a beginner is bound to get a bull's-eye.

00:06:44.450 --> 00:06:46.240
All missiles confirmed hits.

00:06:46.240 --> 00:06:48.580
The target is destroyed.

00:06:48.580 --> 00:06:50.270
Scattered and in free-fall.

00:06:50.550 --> 00:06:53.050
Likelihood of a second
disaster warning rated low.

00:06:55.300 --> 00:06:56.440
What's the matter?

00:06:57.130 --> 00:07:00.490
Nothing, I just had
a bad feeling for a moment.

00:07:00.490 --> 00:07:02.950
But please don't mind me.

00:07:03.170 --> 00:07:07.630
Maybe it's since we've fought
so many of those progressive aliens.

00:07:08.670 --> 00:07:10.950
Where will the fragments land?

00:07:11.110 --> 00:07:15.420
The radius should be along the shore
of Lake Erie in northern Ohio.

00:07:15.580 --> 00:07:17.010
That's pretty close.

00:07:17.010 --> 00:07:20.450
If it were night,
we'd see them as shooting stars.

00:07:29.760 --> 00:07:31.590
Nothing sighted in the crater.

00:07:31.590 --> 00:07:34.100
The parts may have atomized on impact...

00:07:45.740 --> 00:07:46.800
What the?

00:07:46.880 --> 00:07:47.950
H-Hey...

00:08:16.610 --> 00:08:18.370
T-This is nuts!

00:08:26.350 --> 00:08:27.320
It's alive!

00:08:27.380 --> 00:08:28.780
It's still alive!

00:08:37.630 --> 00:08:39.290
The target survived?

00:08:39.360 --> 00:08:40.450
Impossible!

00:08:40.530 --> 00:08:42.010
You're sure that's correct?

00:08:42.170 --> 00:08:46.120
Yes, we're getting a transmission
from the border patrol.

00:08:46.200 --> 00:08:47.970
They're sending real-time video.

00:08:51.740 --> 00:08:52.770
Look at that.

00:08:53.040 --> 00:08:55.270
Like it isn't even hurt.

00:09:51.470 --> 00:09:52.790
<i>Air Force back to B-line.</i>

00:09:52.790 --> 00:09:55.130
It's hitting us at a rate of 70%!

00:09:55.130 --> 00:09:56.720
It's a slaughter.

00:09:56.720 --> 00:09:58.540
As you can see, Captain...

00:09:58.540 --> 00:10:03.010
This one is not only superior in size,
but also recoverability.

00:10:03.310 --> 00:10:05.300
You were right to feel uneasy.

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:08.110
I was hoping I was wrong.

00:10:09.620 --> 00:10:10.610
Moving out.

00:10:17.690 --> 00:10:19.320
Engine, cruise level.

00:10:27.270 --> 00:10:30.000
Mistel clear for takeoff.

00:10:30.070 --> 00:10:32.790
Roger. Mistel T-1, move out!

00:10:42.390 --> 00:10:44.480
Target's projected destination.

00:10:44.550 --> 00:10:45.890
Calculating.

00:10:46.390 --> 00:10:49.720
Of course, there's only
one place it could be headed.

00:10:49.790 --> 00:10:50.990
Commander!

00:10:51.060 --> 00:10:52.190
It can't be!

00:10:59.350 --> 00:11:01.160
How does it look, Captain?

00:11:02.840 --> 00:11:04.820
It's not planning to attack, is it?

00:11:05.110 --> 00:11:07.030
Maybe it’s just a coincidence.

00:11:07.340 --> 00:11:10.580
We don't know its intention,
but we have to stop it.

00:11:10.580 --> 00:11:13.540
HQ will certainly be in danger.

00:11:13.540 --> 00:11:16.710
Pursue and intercept. Prepare for the worst.

00:11:16.710 --> 00:11:20.220
I want you to slow it down
as much as you can.

00:11:20.290 --> 00:11:22.150
Current distance 3000.

00:11:23.120 --> 00:11:27.060
Prepare SARGs 1, 3, and 5
for immediate deployment.

00:11:27.130 --> 00:11:31.730
If we have to, we'll bring in
the EX-1 and attack at close range.

00:11:31.800 --> 00:11:32.770
Understood?

00:11:32.840 --> 00:11:33.800
Yes, sir!

00:11:35.070 --> 00:11:36.560
Lt. Soma?

00:11:36.640 --> 00:11:37.660
Here we go!

00:11:37.740 --> 00:11:38.980
Don't slow us down!

00:11:39.240 --> 00:11:40.940
Roger.

00:11:41.010 --> 00:11:42.450
Lt. Soma?

00:11:42.880 --> 00:11:44.170
Want to switch off?

00:11:44.550 --> 00:11:45.850
I'm all right.

00:11:51.490 --> 00:11:53.850
SARGs 1, 3, and 5, stand by!

00:12:38.300 --> 00:12:39.600
If you were...

00:12:41.970 --> 00:12:43.270
If you were...

00:12:45.040 --> 00:12:47.240
If only you were him...

00:13:00.520 --> 00:13:03.730
Just as I thought,
sniping isn't going to work.

00:13:03.730 --> 00:13:05.370
How's the sound analysis?

00:13:05.730 --> 00:13:08.090
You mean for the Excalibur?

00:13:08.160 --> 00:13:09.560
No good, sir.

00:13:09.630 --> 00:13:12.190
Looks like the surface absorbs shocks.

00:13:15.140 --> 00:13:16.460
Dan and Guenevere!

00:13:22.410 --> 00:13:24.780
We can't do anything from this distance!

00:13:24.780 --> 00:13:26.180
That's right!

00:13:26.250 --> 00:13:27.910
I'm going in first.

00:13:27.980 --> 00:13:29.140
Back me up!

00:13:34.820 --> 00:13:35.790
It's huge!

00:13:45.330 --> 00:13:46.870
If I can get in front of its chest...

00:13:49.050 --> 00:13:50.470
Full auto fire!

00:14:00.250 --> 00:14:03.050
No wonder the sound analysis
wouldn't work...

00:14:19.400 --> 00:14:21.490
What was that just now?

00:14:21.970 --> 00:14:23.630
That attack...

00:14:23.710 --> 00:14:26.680
We've detected a gravitational power shift.

00:14:26.740 --> 00:14:27.940
Gravitational?

00:14:28.010 --> 00:14:29.660
It's an extra reserve of power.

00:14:30.350 --> 00:14:33.250
A giant, internal motor supporting the body.

00:14:33.320 --> 00:14:37.020
Ten times the power that we're used to.

00:14:37.890 --> 00:14:39.340
Lt. Soma?

00:14:39.340 --> 00:14:42.360
If it converts its internal power to external...

00:14:42.430 --> 00:14:45.020
...it can be used as a powerful weapon.

00:14:46.830 --> 00:14:48.800
There's no way we can win.

00:14:48.800 --> 00:14:51.970
It's nothing like any of
the aliens we've seen before.

00:14:52.800 --> 00:14:54.990
We don't need that kind of talk!

00:14:57.940 --> 00:14:59.000
Lieutenant!

00:14:59.000 --> 00:15:00.980
Whose side are you on?

00:15:00.980 --> 00:15:03.740
The aliens or the humans?

00:15:03.740 --> 00:15:05.180
It doesn't matter.

00:15:06.060 --> 00:15:09.150
The monsters should just kill each other.

00:15:09.220 --> 00:15:11.950
We humans aren't in their league.

00:15:12.020 --> 00:15:15.250
I can't even kill that monster I live to hate.

00:15:16.290 --> 00:15:20.010
Then what have you been
fighting for up until now?

00:15:20.160 --> 00:15:22.050
The same thing as everyone else.

00:15:22.330 --> 00:15:24.560
To show that you exist.

00:15:24.560 --> 00:15:26.260
To protect what we have.

00:15:26.260 --> 00:15:27.530
It's always the same.

00:15:27.530 --> 00:15:31.430
Everyone just fights for themselves.

00:15:31.630 --> 00:15:34.340
But I can't even do that...

00:15:34.340 --> 00:15:36.270
Is that all you have to say?

00:15:38.810 --> 00:15:41.110
I'm tired of losing to these things!

00:15:41.380 --> 00:15:44.320
Call it selfishness or whatever!

00:15:44.620 --> 00:15:46.240
He's turning off the limiter?

00:15:47.730 --> 00:15:49.110
I don't care!

00:16:04.370 --> 00:16:05.360
Slug mode!

00:16:06.420 --> 00:16:07.640
Choke on this!

00:16:12.550 --> 00:16:13.610
He did it!

00:16:25.530 --> 00:16:26.500
Dan!

00:16:39.580 --> 00:16:41.880
Lt. Soma, back me up!

00:16:42.240 --> 00:16:43.370
Lieutenant!

00:16:46.650 --> 00:16:47.950
It's no use.

00:17:01.500 --> 00:17:04.260
Are you alive, Lt. Simmons?

00:17:04.330 --> 00:17:05.450
Just barely.

00:17:05.770 --> 00:17:06.930
We're going back.

00:17:07.000 --> 00:17:08.330
Can you fly?

00:17:09.370 --> 00:17:10.740
Roger...

00:17:18.350 --> 00:17:19.610
Mr. Fairy!

00:17:26.060 --> 00:17:28.150
Come on, Mr. Fairy!

00:17:31.490 --> 00:17:32.550
You can do it!

00:17:32.550 --> 00:17:34.060
You can do it, Mr. Fairy!

00:17:58.550 --> 00:18:01.280
Mr. Fairy's punch isn't working.

00:18:01.360 --> 00:18:03.120
No, it is working.

00:18:03.190 --> 00:18:04.390
But...

00:18:04.460 --> 00:18:08.060
It’s just the alien's restoration
is much more effective.

00:18:17.570 --> 00:18:19.700
He can't win?

00:18:27.380 --> 00:18:28.650
No other choice.

00:18:33.960 --> 00:18:35.460
Captain Hartland.

00:18:36.130 --> 00:18:37.790
Get the activation key ready.

00:18:37.790 --> 00:18:38.760
But...

00:18:39.230 --> 00:18:43.390
Both the SARGs and the EX-1
couldn't stop that thing.

00:18:43.470 --> 00:18:44.800
At this rate...

00:18:44.800 --> 00:18:46.200
...HQ will fall.

00:18:47.900 --> 00:18:51.460
This is the only move we have left.

00:18:51.540 --> 00:18:53.300
However...

00:18:53.380 --> 00:18:54.540
That's an order!

00:18:59.980 --> 00:19:00.940
Captain...

00:19:01.320 --> 00:19:03.910
All SARGs, return immediately.

00:19:03.990 --> 00:19:06.750
Prepare for a class 10 nuclear explosion.

00:19:14.660 --> 00:19:16.590
Input emergency recall code.

00:19:16.900 --> 00:19:17.870
But...

00:19:19.270 --> 00:19:20.840
Don't make me say it twice!

00:19:21.900 --> 00:19:23.060
R-Roger.

00:19:25.610 --> 00:19:28.100
Mr. Fairy, I'm with you!

00:19:28.180 --> 00:19:29.300
You can do it!

00:19:35.780 --> 00:19:37.650
A nuclear explosion?

00:19:42.220 --> 00:19:44.120
Didn't you hear, Lieutenant?

00:19:44.120 --> 00:19:45.350
You'll be caught in the blast!

00:19:49.670 --> 00:19:51.060
Just...

00:19:51.130 --> 00:19:55.000
Just like that, my revenge will be complete.

00:19:59.440 --> 00:20:02.380
Are you watching this, Maki?

00:20:06.480 --> 00:20:09.470
Sue, why are you flying so high?

00:20:09.550 --> 00:20:11.750
I can't see Mr. Fairy from here.

00:20:20.230 --> 00:20:23.930
Am I about to get my people killed again?

00:20:27.700 --> 00:20:30.760
We've lost enough.

00:20:30.760 --> 00:20:33.070
I won't let us lose any more.

00:20:34.110 --> 00:20:35.790
On the count of ten.

00:20:35.840 --> 00:20:36.790
10...

00:20:36.790 --> 00:20:37.740
...9...

00:20:37.740 --> 00:20:38.710
...8...

00:20:38.710 --> 00:20:39.670
...7...

00:20:39.670 --> 00:20:40.630
...6...

00:20:40.630 --> 00:20:41.590
...5...

00:20:41.590 --> 00:20:45.350
...4, 3, 2, 1.

00:20:45.420 --> 00:20:46.440
Activate!

00:20:46.480 --> 00:20:47.430
Activate.

00:20:55.760 --> 00:20:56.860
What happened?

00:20:56.890 --> 00:20:58.820
Could it have failed?

00:20:58.820 --> 00:20:59.900
Why?

00:21:06.910 --> 00:21:09.340
Commander, did you turn your key?

00:21:09.410 --> 00:21:10.610
I did!

00:21:10.680 --> 00:21:12.580
Is the activation display lit?

00:21:13.050 --> 00:21:14.610
Trigger system nominal.

00:21:14.680 --> 00:21:16.790
No problem with the Mistel, either.

00:21:17.420 --> 00:21:20.480
Confirmation from the detonator received.

00:21:20.480 --> 00:21:22.220
Confirmation?

00:21:25.960 --> 00:21:27.790
A dummy bomb?

00:21:29.000 --> 00:21:30.930
There wasn't any error...

00:21:40.280 --> 00:21:41.300
I see.

00:21:41.380 --> 00:21:42.910
That's how it is.

00:21:43.180 --> 00:21:47.410
The EX-1 is more important to
the top brass than we are.

00:21:47.720 --> 00:21:50.980
Or they wanted to test our loyalty.

00:21:51.150 --> 00:21:53.200
I guess it doesn't matter.

00:21:53.460 --> 00:21:54.650
It's over.

00:21:54.720 --> 00:21:56.500
It's all over now.

00:21:56.750 --> 00:22:00.100
Anti-alien organization Funeral, huh?

00:22:00.100 --> 00:22:03.970
The reality is that we too are aliens.

00:22:04.470 --> 00:22:06.020
Mr. Fairy...

00:22:06.210 --> 00:22:08.370
Why don't you disappear?

00:22:20.750 --> 00:22:23.010
Why are you...

00:22:24.390 --> 00:22:26.010
...still alive?

00:22:35.560 --> 00:22:38.420
There are those who
awaken sleeping dragons.

00:22:39.130 --> 00:22:41.100
But there are no heroes.

00:22:42.240 --> 00:22:46.400
We will hate each other,
obeying the unspoken rules...

00:22:46.400 --> 00:22:49.140
Next time,
Despair and Hope.
